  },
  "timezone": "browser",
  "tags": [
    "slurm",
    "scenarios"
  ],
  "description": "How a cell gets its colour: the twenty-one Slurm states and the nine colours they resolve to, the same states drawn live, the three continuous modes that colour by occupancy instead of by state, and the shape channel.",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "The states, and the colour each one gets",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 15
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Nine colours for twenty-one states. The hue says what to do about the node; the shade inside a hue says the degree. The state itself is spelled out in the tooltip, in every colour mode.\n\n| | Theme name | What it decides | States it covers |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| <span style=\"display:inline-block;width:30px;height:12px;border-radius:3px;vertical-align:middle;background:#96D98D\"></span> `#96D98D` | `light-green` | **it works** | `allocated, allocated+, allocated-` |\n| <span style=\"display:inline-block;width:30px;height:12px;border-radius:3px;vertical-align:middle;background:#73BF69\"></span> `#73BF69` | `green` | **it works** | `mixed, mix, mixed-` |\n| <span style=\"display:inline-block;width:30px;height:12px;border-radius:3px;vertical-align:middle;background:#56A64B\"></span> `#56A64B` | `semi-dark-green` | **it works** | `completing, comp` |\n| <span style=\"display:inline-block;width:30px;height:12px;border-radius:3px;vertical-align:middle;background:#5794F2\"></span> `#5794F2` | `blue` | **capacity sitting free** | `idle, idle-` |\n| <span style=\"display:inline-block;width:30px;height:12px;border-radius:3px;vertical-align:middle;background:#8AB8FF\"></span> `#8AB8FF` | `light-blue` | **capacity sitting free** | `planned, plnd` |\n| <span style=\"display:inline-block;width:30px;height:12px;border-radius:3px;vertical-align:middle;background:#8F3BB8\"></span> `#8F3BB8` | `dark-purple` | **a human claimed it** | `drained, draining, drng, maintenance, reserved, resv, npc, perfctrs` |\n| <span style=\"display:inline-block;width:30px;height:12px;border-radius:3px;vertical-align:middle;background:#FF9830\"></span> `#FF9830` | `orange` | **not answering, or moving** | `the * suffix, blocked, reboot` |\n| <span style=\"display:inline-block;width:30px;height:12px;border-radius:3px;vertical-align:middle;background:#C4162A\"></span> `#C4162A` | `dark-red` | **broken** | `down, fail, unknown, invalid` |\n| the theme's own ink | `text` | **absent from the floor** | `the ~ suffix, power_down, powering_up, future`, `futr` |\n\nColours are Grafana theme names, so a light or custom theme resolves its own values; the hex above is the dark theme's. What works is drawn light and what is broken dark, because a red-green deficiency collapses the hue and keeps the lightness.\n\n`future` and `futr` are one real state under two spellings: a node declared in slurm.conf that does not exist yet.\n",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        }
      },
      "transparent": false,
      "description": "The nine colours and the states each one covers, as shipped."
    },
    {
